  "id": "mental-map",
  "term": "mental map",
  "definition": "A mental map is an internal representation that can refer either to how a person remembers and represents space and routes, or to a diagram-like organization of ideas and information. In psychology, the term broadly links memory for spaces with symbolic ways of arranging concepts.",
